From 40f6f7c165dae31afd2dbf6efc266a2dd1659e69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:11:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06900/11362] [outer-loop] su15: L9 SOLVED, FULL GAME CLEAR
 (round 7, fable-5)

claude-fable-5 round-7 session cracked su15's L9 -- the seventh attempt
on this frontier, and the game's final level (win_levels=9). The
round-6 near-miss's framing of a "final 7 merge" problem turned out to
be moot: the win condition never required separating the fused hunter
composite from the goal fruit.

Decisive mechanic: a click's drag resolves BEFORE hostile attacks
within the same transition, so towing the goal fruit on every
transition fully suppresses degradation. Baiting all four hunters onto
the kited c fruit made them mass-lunge and fully occlude underneath
it; the complete four-hunter d composite then formed spontaneously
inside that pile with zero explicit choreography. d is itself pullable
like a fruit, and the win fired the instant the c+d stack (d riding
occluded beneath c) was towed into a socket while f already sat in its
own socket. Total cost: 164 actions (19-action continuation past the
145-action L8 prefix), only 18 of 64 meter cells spent.

The source agent's own fresh-reset reproduce() gate confirmed
reached_level=9, and the outer loop independently re-verified
regardless: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new resolver priority
branch, all 5 confirmed level=9, state=GameState.WIN. The game is
fully solved.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: su15 levels_reproduced 8 -> 9,
full_game_clear: true, final_game_state: GameState.WIN.
reproducible_total_levels 159 -> 160 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
